       {
        "name": "api.model_create_multi",
        "arguments": [],
        "options": {}
       }
      ],
      "documentation": "Ensure we correctly assign sequences when creating steps.\nIndeed, sequences are very important within the script, and will break the whole flow if\nnot correctly defined.\n\nThis override will group created steps by chatbot_id and increment the sequence accordingly.\nIt will also look for an existing step for that chatbot and resume from the highest sequence.\n\nThis cannot be done in a default_value for the sequence field as we cannot search by\nrunbot_id.\nIt is also safer and more efficient to do it here (we can batch everything).\n\nIt is still possible to manually pass the 'sequence' in the values, which will take priority. ",
      "size_in_lines": 45,
      "calls_previous_definition": true,
      "validation_messages": []
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "name": "_chatbot_prepare_customer_values",
    "kind": "internal_rule",
    "arguments": [
     "self",
     "discuss_channel",
     "create_partner",
     "update_partner"
    ],
    "definitions": [
     {
      "package": "im_livechat",
      "decorators": [],
      "documentation": "Common method that allows retreiving default customer values from the discuss.channel\nfollowing a chatbot.script.\n\nThis method will return a dict containing the 'customer' values such as:\n{\n    'partner': The created partner (see 'create_partner') or the partner from the\n      environment if not public\n    'email': The email extracted from the discuss.channel messages\n      (see step_type 'question_email')\n    'phone': The phone extracted from the discuss.channel messages\n      (see step_type 'question_phone')\n    'description': A default description containing the \"Please contact me on\" and \"Please\n      call me on\" with the related email and phone numbers.\n      Can be used as a default description to create leads or tickets for example.\n}\n\n:param record discuss_channel: the discuss.channel holding the visitor's conversation with the bot.\n:param bool create_partner: whether or not to create a res.partner is the current user is public.\n  Defaults to True.\n:param bool update_partner: whether or not to set update the email and phone on the res.partner\n  from the environment (if not a public user) if those are not set yet. Defaults to True.\n\n:returns: a dict containing the customer values.",
      "size_in_lines": 65,
      "calls_previous_definition": false,
      "validation_messages": []
     },
     {
      "package": "website_livechat",
      "decorators": [],
      "documentation": null,
      "size_in_lines": 11,
      "calls_previous_definition": true,
      "validation_messages": []
     }
    ]
   },
