   {
    "name": "_process_answer",
    "kind": "background_operation",
    "arguments": [
     "self",
     "discuss_channel",
     "message_body"
    ],
    "definitions": [
     {
      "package": "im_livechat",
      "decorators": [],
      "documentation": "Method called when the user reacts to the current chatbot.script step.\nFor most chatbot.script.step#step_types it simply returns the next chatbot.script.step of\nthe script (see '_fetch_next_step').\n\nSome extra processing is done for steps of type 'question_email' and 'question_phone' where\nwe store the user raw answer (the mail message HTML body) into the chatbot.message in order\nto be able to recover it later (see '_chatbot_prepare_customer_values').\n\n:param discuss_channel:\n:param message_body:\n:return: script step to display next\n:rtype: 'chatbot.script.step' ",
      "size_in_lines": 38,
      "calls_previous_definition": false,
      "validation_messages": [
       {
        "kind": "ValidationError",
        "message": "\"%s\" is not a valid email.",
        "line": 324
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "name": "_process_step",
    "kind": "background_operation",
    "arguments": [
     "self",
     "discuss_channel"
    ],
    "definitions": [
     {
      "package": "im_livechat",
      "decorators": [],
      "documentation": "When we reach a chatbot.step in the script we need to do some processing on behalf of\nthe bot. Which is for most chatbot.script.step#step_types just posting the message field.\n\nSome extra processing may be required for special step types such as 'forward_operator',\n'create_lead', 'create_ticket' (in their related bridge modules).\nThose will have a dedicated processing method with specific docstrings.\n\nReturns the mail.message posted by the chatbot's operator_partner_id. ",
      "size_in_lines": 13,
      "calls_previous_definition": false,
      "validation_messages": []
     },
     {
      "package": "crm_livechat",
      "decorators": [],
      "documentation": null,
